cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SpatiotemporalBench, please cite it as below."
title: "SpatiotemporalBench: spatio-temporal memory of a world perceived through a robot's sensors"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "the SpatiotemporalBench authors"
abstract: >-
  A benchmark of an agent's task-conditioned spatiotemporal ability, perception and memory both: a simulated robot does
  a realistic job (a robot vacuum or a home helper in an apartment, a tote robot in a warehouse, a delivery drone over a
  downtown district) in a photoreal, changing place, and an agent that keeps its own memory is streamed what the
  robot's sensors recorded and asked the questions a controller would ask itself, during the job and after it. Gold
  answers are computed by code from the simulator's full record of the world, and validity gates over scripted
  baselines keep out question families that shortcuts can answer.
version: 0.11.1
date-released: 2026-10-30
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/DanMcInerney/SpatiotemporalBench"
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - robotics
  - memory
  - spatial reasoning
  - embodied AI
